WEBVTT

00:01.335 --> 00:03.337
[♪ theme music playing]

00:29.154 --> 00:30.197
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

00:33.283 --> 00:34.826
CHARACTERS, EVENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND PLACES IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

00:34.910 --> 00:36.203
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

00:37.579 --> 00:38.580
I found you.

00:39.831 --> 00:41.041
[♪ pleasant music playing]

00:46.672 --> 00:47.714
This is bad.

00:57.641 --> 00:59.643
[♪ uplifting song playing]

01:08.402 --> 01:10.028
Why are you…

01:11.113 --> 01:12.447
I'm just copying you.

01:14.449 --> 01:16.994
I have a habit of copying other people.

01:19.830 --> 01:20.914
[sighs]

01:21.582 --> 01:24.793
-[stammers] But I can't breathe…
-Oh.

01:26.295 --> 01:27.296
Sorry.

01:27.379 --> 01:28.922
[chuckles awkwardly, clears throat]

01:29.506 --> 01:32.467
You said you hug people
you're happy to see.

01:39.891 --> 01:40.892
[♪ song ends]

01:41.852 --> 01:43.562
EPISODE 7

01:43.645 --> 01:44.938
[indicator clicking]

01:45.022 --> 01:46.690
[driver clicks tongue, sighs]

01:51.778 --> 01:52.779
[car thuds]

02:03.457 --> 02:05.000
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

02:06.543 --> 02:07.544
[Chan clears throat]

02:18.430 --> 02:19.890
We're here.

02:21.725 --> 02:22.726
Sir?

02:23.560 --> 02:24.603
Yes?

02:31.318 --> 02:32.736
Can you open the trunk?

02:32.819 --> 02:35.656
Just keep riding this to SHIM.
Mr. Park will be waiting.

02:40.911 --> 02:41.912
[♪ music ends]

02:44.373 --> 02:45.374
[sighs]

02:49.628 --> 02:50.629
Ah.

02:51.380 --> 02:52.547
Yes, Mr. Yeon.

02:53.131 --> 02:54.299
Producer Ben?

02:54.383 --> 02:55.801
[Yeon] He just informed me

02:55.884 --> 02:57.969
that the collaboration project
will resume.

03:01.056 --> 03:02.182
Huh?

03:03.850 --> 03:05.310
[Haran gasps, chuckles]

03:05.394 --> 03:07.896
[Yeon] The animation team
will return to Korea soon.

03:07.979 --> 03:10.190
All right. That's good.

03:10.273 --> 03:12.150
-[♪ lighthearted music playing]
-[chuckles]

03:15.696 --> 03:17.364
[grunts, pants]

03:17.447 --> 03:18.615
[Manjae] My roommate!

03:19.449 --> 03:21.034
[Chan] Oh. Mr. Park!

03:21.576 --> 03:22.953
Mr. Park.

03:23.036 --> 03:24.746
How have you been?

03:24.830 --> 03:26.248
Sorry, I couldn't call you.

03:28.583 --> 03:29.876
You're here, so it's fine.

03:29.960 --> 03:32.254
Why are you standing out here in the cold?

03:32.337 --> 03:34.005
You didn't know when I'd get here.

03:34.089 --> 03:35.882
I just came out 10 seconds ago.

03:37.592 --> 03:39.761
Goodness. But look at you…

03:40.429 --> 03:43.974
You must have been through a lot.
You look so gaunt.

03:44.057 --> 03:45.600
Do I?

03:45.684 --> 03:47.144
[groans] That's awful.

03:47.727 --> 03:48.854
I should get prettier now.

03:48.937 --> 03:50.730
[chuckles, stutters]

03:50.814 --> 03:52.649
You didn't forget your meds, right?

03:52.732 --> 03:54.568
And your cardiac enzyme levels?

03:55.318 --> 03:56.987
It's cold. Let's go inside.

03:57.070 --> 04:00.240
-Genius, Chan is here. Come on in.
-[Genius barks]

04:00.323 --> 04:02.492
-It's cold.
-Are you running away?

04:02.576 --> 04:03.869
Mr. Park!

04:04.536 --> 04:06.788
-[exclaims] Genius!
-[whines]

04:06.872 --> 04:07.914
Genius.

04:07.998 --> 04:09.833
-[♪ pleasant music playing]
-[whines]

04:09.916 --> 04:12.961
Hey, Genius.
Aren't you going to show me your face?

04:13.545 --> 04:14.796
Hey, Grouchy.

04:14.880 --> 04:17.883
You were waiting for Chan the whole time.
Are you protesting?

04:17.966 --> 04:20.051
[sighs] Leave him.

04:20.552 --> 04:22.679
He's sour because you left
without telling him.

04:23.180 --> 04:24.598
Go upstairs. You must be tired.

04:26.933 --> 04:27.934
[♪ music fades]

04:28.018 --> 04:29.895
[groans]

04:29.978 --> 04:31.354
[sighs]

04:32.564 --> 04:33.565
[sighs]

04:41.448 --> 04:42.449
[wooden thud]

04:42.532 --> 04:44.868
Oh… Yes, Mr. Park. Come in.

04:46.912 --> 04:47.913
[grunts softly]

04:48.538 --> 04:49.539
-[Genius barks]
-Oh?

04:51.166 --> 04:53.335
-Genius. [chuckles]
-[whines]

04:53.418 --> 04:56.505
Want to sleep with me today?
Hmm? [chuckles]

04:58.215 --> 05:00.550
Dogs should sleep at this hour.

05:01.176 --> 05:02.177
Hmm?

05:02.677 --> 05:03.804
Me?

05:05.305 --> 05:07.474
I have a lot on my mind.

05:08.642 --> 05:13.605
Genius, you know
that Haran should become happy, right?

05:14.856 --> 05:17.734
That's all I wanted for her,

05:19.277 --> 05:20.821
but what do I do now?

05:21.988 --> 05:23.031
[♪ mellow music playing]

05:23.114 --> 05:26.576
I want her to be happy beside me,

05:29.621 --> 05:32.165
and I want her to be happy because of me.

05:33.333 --> 05:35.043
I keep getting greedy.

05:36.211 --> 05:38.296
IF IT'S OKAY WITH YOU, YOU CAN TALK TO ME

05:38.380 --> 05:42.425
The fact that I was fake,
and the reason I became a fake…

05:43.218 --> 05:48.890
The fact that I lived
while he died from that accident…

05:52.727 --> 05:57.315
I keep wanting to do as I want

05:58.441 --> 05:59.860
as if I'm clueless to all that.

06:02.320 --> 06:03.989
Until I go back,

06:05.115 --> 06:08.702
if I play dumb and be greedy,

06:09.911 --> 06:11.162
would that be wrong?

06:12.163 --> 06:13.790
[wind whooshing]

06:13.874 --> 06:17.085
-[leaves rustling]
-[bird chirping]

06:17.168 --> 06:19.087
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

06:19.170 --> 06:20.839
[♪ music fades]

06:20.922 --> 06:22.507
[Chan] Here's today's dress code.

06:22.924 --> 06:24.926
Comfy shoes and warm clothes.

06:25.719 --> 06:26.803
See you later.

06:26.887 --> 06:28.805
I can't travel too far today.

06:30.473 --> 06:31.474
CLOSED DUE TO PERSONAL REASONS

06:31.558 --> 06:32.559
Oh?

06:33.727 --> 06:34.769
Hmm?

06:35.353 --> 06:37.188
-[lively chatter]
-Mr. Park…

06:38.273 --> 06:39.858
-Oh! Ms. Song.
-Ms. Song.

06:39.941 --> 06:41.443
-Hey.
-Hello.

06:41.526 --> 06:42.527
[Haran] What are you all doing…

06:43.194 --> 06:44.696
Ben, when did you get here?

06:44.779 --> 06:45.780
Have you been well?

06:45.864 --> 06:48.325
I visited as soon as I arrived,
and now I'm trapped.

06:48.408 --> 06:49.409
[laughter]

06:49.492 --> 06:51.828
We came when we saw Seunggyu's photo
in our group chat.

06:51.911 --> 06:54.706
I wanted to get the coffee
you bought us last time,

06:54.789 --> 06:57.125
-and I saw that Chan was here.
-[chuckles softly]

06:57.208 --> 07:00.962
As soon as I saw the photo,
I rushed over with my sheet mask still on.

07:01.046 --> 07:03.381
Things worked out,
so he's staying for two months.

07:03.465 --> 07:04.758
Isn't that great?

07:04.841 --> 07:06.551
Right…

07:06.635 --> 07:07.719
[toy] Let's play.

07:07.802 --> 07:08.970
Let's play.

07:09.054 --> 07:11.598
Oh, I gave them to Genius as a gift.

07:11.681 --> 07:15.060
If he presses the buttons,
we can communicate.

07:15.143 --> 07:17.354
I have soccer class,
so I'll be back later.

07:17.437 --> 07:19.481
-Bye.
-Bye.

07:19.564 --> 07:20.649
[both chuckle]

07:20.732 --> 07:22.275
-Bye.
-[everyone] Bye, Donggu.

07:22.359 --> 07:23.360
[Chan] Bye.

07:23.443 --> 07:25.487
-See you later.
-Ms. Song, sit down.

07:25.570 --> 07:26.655
Right.

07:26.738 --> 07:29.949
We'll need some wine for a welcome party.

07:30.033 --> 07:31.868
Roomie, please get the wine glasses.

07:31.951 --> 07:33.161
-Sure.
-[all cheering]

07:33.244 --> 07:36.831
-Mom, I'm going home late today!
-[laughter]

07:36.915 --> 07:40.043
[Sol] Raemee, you live with your mother?
Not alone?

07:40.877 --> 07:42.545
-[sighs]
-[laughter]

07:42.629 --> 07:44.631
[indistinct chatter]

07:52.555 --> 07:54.474
[metallic clink echoing]

07:55.016 --> 07:56.142
Can I help with anything?

07:57.602 --> 07:59.062
What? Oh…

08:00.355 --> 08:02.649
Ah. It's okay. Sit down.

08:05.360 --> 08:07.153
[♪ foreboding music plays]

08:13.201 --> 08:14.411
[♪ music fades]

08:16.871 --> 08:18.331
Please let us clean up.

08:18.415 --> 08:19.541
Please.

08:19.624 --> 08:21.584
The host should clean up.

08:21.668 --> 08:24.129
-Just come have some coffee next time.
-[Sol groans]

08:24.212 --> 08:25.296
-[Hayeong] Okay.
-[Pureum] All right.

08:25.380 --> 08:27.549
-[Sol] Then, we'll come have coffee.
-[Manjae] Okay, thank you.

08:27.632 --> 08:29.843
[everyone] Thank you.

08:29.926 --> 08:33.722
Still, shouldn't at least one of us
stay back and help clean up?

08:33.805 --> 08:35.932
We're going for another round,

08:36.015 --> 08:38.727
so you can help out here, Lightweight.

08:38.810 --> 08:40.186
-Me?
-Yes, you. Song Haran.

08:40.270 --> 08:41.604
-The lightweight.
-Ah.

08:41.688 --> 08:43.064
Then I'll stay and help too…

08:43.148 --> 08:45.066
Come on. You'll just break the cups.

08:45.150 --> 08:46.735
We'll come back next time. Bye.

08:46.818 --> 08:48.319
-See you next time.
-Okay, bye.

08:48.403 --> 08:50.071
-[Sol] I should--
-[Raemee] Let's go.

08:50.780 --> 08:52.032
[Manjae chuckles]

08:52.115 --> 08:53.908
My gosh.

08:53.992 --> 08:54.993
[whines]

08:56.036 --> 08:59.247
[inhales sharply] I didn't expect them
to all swarm in here.

08:59.748 --> 09:00.749
Yeah.

09:02.542 --> 09:04.669
[♪ whimsical music playing]

09:04.753 --> 09:07.172
Sorry. We're going to drink this later.

09:07.255 --> 09:08.256
[Chan chuckles]

09:10.216 --> 09:13.511
But it's suddenly so quiet
with all of them gone.

09:14.262 --> 09:16.556
Right. It was pretty noisy in here.

09:17.223 --> 09:18.308
But, Ms. Song--

09:18.391 --> 09:19.601
[toy] I love you.

09:19.684 --> 09:20.685
[♪ music fades]

09:22.937 --> 09:25.315
-[laughing]
-[clears throat]

09:25.398 --> 09:28.777
Genius, you shouldn't just
keep pressing those.

09:28.860 --> 09:30.737
[clears throat] What I meant to say is…

09:30.820 --> 09:31.821
[toy] I love you.

09:32.322 --> 09:33.948
[♪ whimsical music continues]

09:35.450 --> 09:38.620
[chuckles awkwardly]
Has he not been trained yet?

09:38.703 --> 09:40.622
I was trying to say

09:41.122 --> 09:44.167
that I thought you'd be startled
to see everyone here,

09:44.250 --> 09:46.669
so I sent you a message.

09:46.753 --> 09:49.756
-[chuckling awkwardly] Oh. I see.
-[♪ music fades]

09:49.839 --> 09:52.425
[Manjae exclaims] I'm so full.

09:52.509 --> 09:54.719
I'm going to take a walk with Genius.

09:54.803 --> 09:56.429
You can clean up the rest, right?

09:56.513 --> 09:57.889
Sure. Ms. Song and I--

09:57.972 --> 09:59.933
-[toy] I love you.
-[♪ music continues]

10:00.016 --> 10:01.601
[Manjae exclaims] Oops.

10:01.684 --> 10:02.894
My mistake. [chuckles]

10:02.977 --> 10:04.062
[chuckles softly]

10:04.145 --> 10:05.688
See you later. Let's go.

10:09.359 --> 10:10.401
[clears throat]

10:10.485 --> 10:13.071
[chuckles] Let's clean this up, then.

10:14.614 --> 10:16.157
[Haran exclaims, gasps]

10:16.241 --> 10:17.575
You got it on your sleeve.

10:17.659 --> 10:19.994
It'll get stained
if you don't wash it off.

10:21.162 --> 10:23.289
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

10:26.042 --> 10:27.085
-[♪ music stops]
-[stammers]

10:28.336 --> 10:29.879
I'll go get changed.

10:31.297 --> 10:34.384
[chuckles nervously, clears throat]

10:35.760 --> 10:38.179
[groans] Training on the weekend?

10:38.263 --> 10:39.848
I'm wasting my youth.

10:41.474 --> 10:43.101
Oh? It's Song Hadam.

10:43.184 --> 10:44.727
Oh? It's Cha Yougyum.

10:50.817 --> 10:51.985
Hi.

10:52.068 --> 10:53.486
I'm Kim Seokhyeon from Class 1.

10:53.570 --> 10:55.488
I've been interested in you,

10:55.572 --> 10:57.991
but I don't have to give up
because of Yougyum now.

10:59.075 --> 11:00.285
Can I have your number?

11:00.368 --> 11:02.287
Hey, what is he saying?

11:02.871 --> 11:04.497
Did you two break up?

11:04.998 --> 11:07.542
[Hadam] Cha Yougyum,
are you just going to watch?

11:07.625 --> 11:10.753
If you don't come until I count to three,
I'm giving him my number.

11:10.837 --> 11:13.548
One, two…

11:14.299 --> 11:16.301
[♪ dramatic music playing]

11:17.177 --> 11:18.720
All right. I'll give it to you.

11:23.433 --> 11:24.642
Text me.

11:31.107 --> 11:32.984
-[boys exclaim teasingly]
-[student 1] You got her number.

11:33.067 --> 11:35.403
-[boy 2] What's this?
-[boy 1] What?

11:35.486 --> 11:38.239
-Please call me if you see her.
-[passersby talk indistinctly]

11:38.323 --> 11:41.534
If you ever see my mother,
please give me a call.

11:41.618 --> 11:43.077
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

11:46.664 --> 11:47.916
[Manjae] Kim Nabong.

11:49.000 --> 11:50.501
[Nana] Hey, Manjae.

11:51.377 --> 11:52.587
Park Genius.

11:52.670 --> 11:55.506
-[chuckles]
-[exclaims] Genius, how have you been?

11:55.590 --> 11:57.091
Were you taking a walk?

11:57.175 --> 11:59.302
Yes, this is a good place to work out.

11:59.385 --> 12:01.721
-I walk a few laps every day.
-No way.

12:01.804 --> 12:03.973
I walk him every day here, too.

12:04.057 --> 12:07.644
Well, I guess we wouldn't have
recognized each other until now.

12:07.727 --> 12:08.728
[both chuckle]

12:08.811 --> 12:11.147
We can be walking buddies from now on.

12:11.231 --> 12:12.315
[barks, whines]

12:12.398 --> 12:13.483
Hey.

12:13.566 --> 12:15.026
I think he needs to poop.

12:15.109 --> 12:17.237
-He has his own poop area over there.
-[Genius barks]

12:17.320 --> 12:18.780
-Gosh.
-Go and let him poop.

12:18.863 --> 12:20.990
-Okay, I'll see you later.
-[laughs]

12:21.074 --> 12:22.992
Hey, Genius! Slow down.

12:23.076 --> 12:24.744
All right. Goodness.

12:24.827 --> 12:26.746
Slow down. Okay.

12:30.750 --> 12:32.252
[♪ mysterious music playing]

12:33.044 --> 12:35.880
[Manjae] What was she doing here?

12:35.964 --> 12:39.092
-Are you sick or anything?
-I was just visiting a friend there.

12:45.223 --> 12:47.141
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

12:53.064 --> 12:54.065
[♪ music ends]

12:57.318 --> 12:58.736
[Nana] Is that you, Yougyum?

13:02.907 --> 13:03.992
Hello.

13:05.118 --> 13:06.869
Why are you wearing glasses?

13:06.953 --> 13:08.621
-I almost didn't recognize you.
-[sniffles]

13:08.705 --> 13:10.331
My eyes are swollen.

13:10.415 --> 13:11.666
How swollen can they be?

13:12.333 --> 13:16.004
[gasps] My goodness.
They really are incredibly puffy.

13:16.087 --> 13:17.880
How did your eyes get like…

13:19.132 --> 13:20.466
-Are you crying?
-[sobbing]

13:22.677 --> 13:25.221
I had a fight with Hadam,

13:25.305 --> 13:27.724
and it feels like
my whole world just fell apart.

13:29.851 --> 13:33.187
How do I live from now on, Ms. Kim?

13:35.481 --> 13:36.482
Follow me.

13:37.525 --> 13:39.444
What? Where…

13:43.823 --> 13:47.243
Fighting won't make the world fall apart.
It only exhausts you.

13:47.326 --> 13:48.369
Eat up.

13:48.953 --> 13:50.496
I don't have an appetite.

13:50.580 --> 13:54.500
To me, Hadam is my whole world
and my whole universe… [groans]

13:55.334 --> 13:57.587
You're out. Just break up with Hadam.

13:58.171 --> 13:59.630
-What?
-I'm not letting a guy

13:59.714 --> 14:02.425
who bawls after one fight
about the world falling apart

14:02.508 --> 14:03.760
date my granddaughter.

14:03.843 --> 14:06.179
How will you survive the big leagues
with that mentality?

14:06.262 --> 14:07.889
You're out.

14:08.473 --> 14:09.766
No…

14:10.516 --> 14:11.684
I'll eat.

14:13.519 --> 14:14.896
[yelps] Too hot!

14:15.772 --> 14:19.275
I'm only weak when it comes to Hadam.
I push myself hard when I'm training.

14:19.358 --> 14:21.319
I'm the ruthless Cha Yougyum.

14:24.322 --> 14:28.451
Right. At your age, you think the world
falls apart with the smallest things.

14:29.577 --> 14:30.703
I did, too.

14:32.622 --> 14:36.584
But once you go through
something really serious,

14:36.667 --> 14:40.880
you'll realize
that the issues you thought were huge

14:40.963 --> 14:43.132
were actually just tiny specks.

14:43.216 --> 14:47.303
And you'll regret not facing
those issues head-on back then.

14:47.386 --> 14:49.639
You'll think, "Why was I such a coward?"

14:50.765 --> 14:54.310
Anyway, there are dozens of more serious
problems waiting for you in life.

14:54.393 --> 14:55.895
So stop being weak.

14:56.979 --> 14:58.106
Okay.

14:59.357 --> 15:02.693
I'm sorry.
I was absorbed in my own issues.

15:03.402 --> 15:04.862
Ah. What about your checkup?

15:04.946 --> 15:08.282
Something came up at work,
so I rescheduled. [chuckles]

15:08.366 --> 15:10.701
I got scolded
for disappearing from the hospital.

15:10.785 --> 15:12.995
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

15:14.413 --> 15:15.623
[sniffles]

15:17.708 --> 15:20.878
I learned that abalones contain ta…

15:21.712 --> 15:22.880
Ta…

15:22.964 --> 15:24.048
Taurine.

15:24.132 --> 15:26.884
They contain taurine,
which helps with cognitive function.

15:28.970 --> 15:31.389
All right. Give me all the abalones.

15:32.557 --> 15:35.143
I still have a lot to do,
so I have to stay strong.

15:35.226 --> 15:38.604
You eat up, too.
You need the energy to make up with Hadam.

15:38.688 --> 15:40.106
Right. Energy.

15:40.189 --> 15:41.941
[chuckling]

15:42.775 --> 15:44.986
[slurps] Gosh, that's hot.
[inhales sharply]

15:45.069 --> 15:47.446
[both laughing]

15:47.530 --> 15:48.531
[♪ music fades]

15:52.285 --> 15:53.870
-[sighs]
-[cell phone vibrating]

15:56.622 --> 15:58.332
[cell phone continues vibrating]

15:59.917 --> 16:01.419
Mr. Seonu.

16:01.502 --> 16:03.504
[cell phone continues vibrating]

16:04.755 --> 16:07.633
Mr. Seonu, there's someone calling you.

16:11.429 --> 16:14.557
[knocks on door] Someone keeps calling…

16:15.766 --> 16:16.934
Is he not here?

16:18.769 --> 16:20.438
-[Haran squeals] I'm sorry.
-[Chan exclaims]

16:21.272 --> 16:22.315
Right.

16:23.065 --> 16:25.234
[stutters] What is it?

16:25.318 --> 16:26.527
I…

16:26.611 --> 16:27.987
[hesitates]

16:28.070 --> 16:30.865
Someone kept calling,
so it seemed important.

16:31.616 --> 16:33.868
-I'm sorry.
-Wait.

16:33.951 --> 16:35.411
Yes?

16:35.494 --> 16:36.495
I mean…

16:39.457 --> 16:40.917
[♪ heart-fluttering music playing]

16:46.631 --> 16:50.218
[stutters] We shouldn't do it here…

16:50.801 --> 16:52.053
-I mean…
-No, I…

16:56.098 --> 16:58.476
-Why are you turning off the lights?
-You…

17:05.816 --> 17:06.817
[♪ music ends]

17:06.901 --> 17:08.778
You're the one who turned them off.

17:11.405 --> 17:12.615
With your back.

17:15.159 --> 17:17.411
Oh. My back… [chuckles awkwardly]

17:17.495 --> 17:18.955
You've got something on your lips.

17:19.038 --> 17:21.624
-[exclaims softly]
-Crumbs or something.

17:21.707 --> 17:23.960
[groans] It was the crackers…

17:24.627 --> 17:25.962
-[Haran clears throat]
-[inhales sharply]

17:26.045 --> 17:28.214
But why did you close your eyes?

17:28.297 --> 17:29.298
[clears throat]

17:31.133 --> 17:34.720
[stutters] Honestly, anyone would have
misunderstood that situation.

17:34.804 --> 17:38.182
You held my hand and hugged me yesterday,
so I thought…

17:38.266 --> 17:39.392
You thought what?

17:40.476 --> 17:43.938
I just thought you were moving fast
since you're from the States.

17:44.438 --> 17:46.315
[groans] This is getting weird.

17:46.816 --> 17:48.442
-Stop teasing me.
-[Chan exclaims]

17:48.526 --> 17:49.735
I wasn't teasing you.

17:49.819 --> 17:52.154
I just thought I saw the old you.

17:52.863 --> 17:54.115
It was cute. [chuckles]

17:54.198 --> 17:55.575
My old self?

17:55.658 --> 17:57.493
What do you mean?

18:00.246 --> 18:02.582
I think I heard you used to be
much more cheerful.

18:03.374 --> 18:04.375
From who?

18:05.293 --> 18:06.544
Was it Hayeong?

18:07.336 --> 18:10.464
[stutters] Anyway,
I really wasn't teasing you.

18:10.965 --> 18:12.883
[chuckles softly] I'm sorry.

18:14.010 --> 18:15.052
[sighs]

18:15.136 --> 18:17.805
Ah. I forgot to give you this.

18:18.973 --> 18:20.141
[in English] A welcome drink.

18:21.851 --> 18:24.145
[in Korean] I almost took back my word
about being nice to you.

18:26.689 --> 18:28.232
Can we do it now?

18:28.983 --> 18:29.984
Do what?

18:30.901 --> 18:32.695
[stutters] I meant…

18:32.778 --> 18:34.614
The photos.

18:34.697 --> 18:35.990
Let's check your homework.

18:37.366 --> 18:38.367
[both chuckle]

18:39.619 --> 18:41.621
[♪ lighthearted music playing]

18:44.957 --> 18:46.167
[Chan hums in approval]

18:46.751 --> 18:49.545
[inhales sharply]
You have a talent for this. [chuckles]

18:50.171 --> 18:52.298
Oh, my gosh.

18:53.382 --> 18:55.051
-[exclaims]
-[sighs]

18:55.134 --> 18:57.386
You liar.
You said there were just 10 shots.

18:59.889 --> 19:03.225
Hmm? My Destinations List…

19:03.309 --> 19:06.062
It's yours. I took a photo of it.

19:07.063 --> 19:09.565
-When did you take this?
-What?

19:10.107 --> 19:11.233
This!

19:11.317 --> 19:15.738
[stutters] I just took this for fun
when I was bored…

19:15.821 --> 19:17.823
Wow. That's not fair.

19:18.491 --> 19:20.034
You promised to do that with me.

19:21.035 --> 19:22.703
That doesn't count. I'm confiscating this.

19:22.787 --> 19:24.538
-[exclaims]
-Everything you did alone is invalid.

19:24.622 --> 19:26.582
We'll do everything together.

19:26.666 --> 19:28.584
[scoffs] Geez.

19:30.044 --> 19:33.673
But what's that last thing
you scribbled out?

19:33.756 --> 19:36.634
[Chan] Mmm. [inhales sharply]

19:37.301 --> 19:40.763
I thought it would be impossible,
so I scribbled it out…

19:44.892 --> 19:46.227
but it might be possible now.

19:47.812 --> 19:49.146
It's a secret, though.

19:52.650 --> 19:55.111
Why did you tell me
to wear comfy shoes today?

19:55.194 --> 19:58.489
I thought we'd just walk around a bit

19:58.572 --> 20:00.366
without any specific plans.

20:00.449 --> 20:02.201
Just go wherever the wind takes us?

20:02.284 --> 20:03.285
[chuckles softly]

20:03.661 --> 20:05.871
I wanted to try that with you.

20:06.497 --> 20:07.957
Go somewhere and try things

20:08.040 --> 20:11.335
without thinking of what happens next.

20:12.503 --> 20:13.546
No,

20:14.505 --> 20:16.632
that may have messed things up.

20:17.425 --> 20:21.095
If things get messed up, we can fix them.
It's the same for knots.

20:21.929 --> 20:24.807
Sometimes they seem impossible to undo,

20:25.307 --> 20:28.602
but if you loosen one strand at a time,
they'll unravel. [chuckles softly]

20:29.937 --> 20:32.857
You can find a way,
no matter how impossible it seems.

20:35.943 --> 20:37.445
Shall we do it tomorrow?

20:38.195 --> 20:40.990
Try going wherever the wind takes us.

20:41.782 --> 20:43.200
-Sorry. Next time.
-[♪ music fades]

20:43.284 --> 20:46.370
I have to go somewhere far
with my family tomorrow.

20:46.454 --> 20:47.913
Far? Where?

20:51.459 --> 20:52.460
Ah.

20:53.377 --> 20:54.712
THE LATE SONG JUNHO
THE LATE MIN HYEWON

20:54.795 --> 20:58.090
[Hayeong] Dad's favorite crab stew.

20:59.425 --> 21:00.426
[grunts]

21:00.509 --> 21:03.721
Remember when Dad chipped his tooth
eating crab stew?

21:03.804 --> 21:06.724
Right, he visited the dentist
for a long time after that. [laughs]

21:08.100 --> 21:09.685
Hadam, wait.

21:09.769 --> 21:12.480
Put the castella on Mom's favorite dish.

21:13.272 --> 21:16.859
[Hayeong] Wow. That's a real antique.
We've had that since I was a baby.

21:16.942 --> 21:19.737
Whenever we were in a bad mood,
she gave us snacks on this.

21:19.820 --> 21:21.489
Mom always said,

21:21.572 --> 21:25.451
"When you're feeling down,
having sweets on a pretty dish

21:25.534 --> 21:27.703
-will make you feel sparkly."
-Sparkly.

21:27.787 --> 21:29.872
[Hayeong, Haran, and Nana laugh]

21:31.040 --> 21:33.042
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

21:35.044 --> 21:36.712
-[Nana] Let's greet them now.
-[Hayeong] Okay.

21:41.342 --> 21:45.054
[Nana] This might be
my last time coming here.

21:46.680 --> 21:47.890
If, by any chance,

21:47.973 --> 21:51.268
I start acting too strange,
just call me home to you quickly.

21:51.852 --> 21:54.855
I don't want to embarrass myself
in front of them.

21:55.523 --> 21:56.649
Okay, Hyewon?

21:57.566 --> 21:58.776
Okay, Junho?

22:06.784 --> 22:09.703
I will take you all home safely.

22:09.787 --> 22:10.996
-Let's go.
-[♪ music fades]

22:11.705 --> 22:12.706
[tires screech]

22:13.791 --> 22:18.629
[singsongs] Ah…
My bad feelings are never wrong.

22:18.712 --> 22:19.713
I forgot my phone.

22:21.257 --> 22:23.551
-I'm riding with Haran.
-Eh?

22:23.634 --> 22:26.345
You're really going to betray me? Hey!

22:27.763 --> 22:28.806
[Hayeong scoffs]

22:28.889 --> 22:30.641
She's so cold.

22:31.851 --> 22:34.395
[sings in English in tune of Für Elise]
♪ I dream a little bit of red alone ♪

22:41.193 --> 22:42.611
[Hayeong in Korean] No, I had it then.

22:42.695 --> 22:43.904
And then, Grandma…

22:43.988 --> 22:47.283
I greeted Mom and Dad,
then I got up, and my phone…

22:47.741 --> 22:49.243
[sighs exasperatedly]
Where did I leave it?

22:50.744 --> 22:51.829
-[man] I'm really sorry.
-Eh?

22:51.912 --> 22:52.913
Who's that?

22:52.997 --> 22:54.164
[man] I'm sorry.

22:54.248 --> 22:56.834
Excuse me, that's my parents' grave.

22:56.917 --> 22:58.711
I think you came to the wrong…

23:00.754 --> 23:01.964
Mr. Yeon?

23:02.590 --> 23:03.883
Why are you…

23:05.009 --> 23:06.010
Are you crying?

23:06.093 --> 23:08.137
Oh… No.

23:08.220 --> 23:10.639
You are. Your eyes are red.

23:11.181 --> 23:13.267
[scoffs] People would think
you're their son…

23:15.352 --> 23:17.479
[♪ emotional music playing]

23:17.563 --> 23:18.689
Thank you.

23:19.773 --> 23:21.317
[Hyewon] How pretty.

23:21.400 --> 23:24.028
You don't need to do this
for Parents' Day.

23:24.111 --> 23:27.239
You always welcome me
and pack me side dishes.

23:27.323 --> 23:30.242
I'm a bit awkward
with expressing my feelings,

23:30.326 --> 23:32.703
but I really wanted to thank you today.

23:32.786 --> 23:34.204
[exclaims softly]

23:34.288 --> 23:35.789
Goodness. Thank you.

23:35.873 --> 23:37.708
My friends brag about their sons.

23:37.791 --> 23:40.502
I can brag to them that I got
carnations from my son, too.

23:40.586 --> 23:41.629
[all chuckle]

23:41.712 --> 23:45.174
Since we're all dressed up,
how about a family photo?

23:45.257 --> 23:46.717
That sounds great.

23:46.800 --> 23:48.594
-Let's take a photo over there.
-Okay.

23:48.677 --> 23:51.597
-Oh, sure.
-[Junho] Let's take a photo.

23:51.680 --> 23:53.599
-All right.
-[Hyewon] Mr. Yeon.

23:53.682 --> 23:55.893
-Let's take it together.
-Come on, Mr. Yeon.

23:55.976 --> 23:57.519
-Join us.
-Come here.

23:57.603 --> 23:59.021
It's okay.

23:59.104 --> 24:01.023
It's a family photo. Come here.

24:01.106 --> 24:03.943
Sir, can you take a photo of us?

24:05.486 --> 24:06.612
[man] All right.

24:06.695 --> 24:08.197
One, two, three.

24:08.280 --> 24:09.281
[camera clicks]

24:18.248 --> 24:19.708
[sighs] Mom, Dad.

24:19.792 --> 24:22.711
Our former chauffeur, Mr. Yeon,
became our COO.

24:22.795 --> 24:26.924
He's a core figure now,
like me in our household.

24:27.508 --> 24:30.052
So send him lots of energy.

24:33.973 --> 24:35.683
Thank you for taking care

24:36.934 --> 24:38.477
of our parents, too.

24:41.438 --> 24:42.439
-I'm sorry.
-[♪ music ends]

24:42.898 --> 24:45.526
Why do you keep saying sorry?

24:45.609 --> 24:46.610
I…

24:48.404 --> 24:50.030
I'm really sorry.

24:53.575 --> 24:56.662
Oh. I dropped my phone somewhere.

24:56.745 --> 24:58.205
Can you call my number?

25:01.834 --> 25:03.919
-[sniffs] Where is it?
-[cell phone ringing]

25:04.003 --> 25:05.921
I hear it. Where is it?

25:07.131 --> 25:08.966
Is it here? Is it here?

25:09.550 --> 25:10.551
Is it here?

25:10.634 --> 25:11.635
[Yeon] I…

25:12.803 --> 25:14.304
It's coming from your butt.

25:15.014 --> 25:16.849
-My butt?
-[ringing stops]

25:17.474 --> 25:21.020
Darn it. I came all the way
back up here for nothing.

25:21.770 --> 25:24.773
[sighs heavily] Since we met here,

25:25.566 --> 25:26.817
should we go eat something?

25:27.234 --> 25:28.235
Eat?

25:28.318 --> 25:30.487
I promised you I'd treat you last time.

25:30.571 --> 25:34.116
It was 39,000 won last time,

25:35.701 --> 25:38.412
so I'll treat you to up to 80,000 won.

25:38.495 --> 25:41.457
[gasps] There's an amazing
oxtail soup place nearby.

25:41.540 --> 25:42.541
What do you say?

25:42.624 --> 25:43.792
Let's go!

25:43.876 --> 25:45.753
[Yeon hesitates] It's okay…

25:45.836 --> 25:47.379
No, it's not okay.

25:48.005 --> 25:49.840
Have we eaten together before?

25:49.923 --> 25:51.967
Who do you normally
have lunch with at work?

25:52.051 --> 25:54.595
What do you usually do on the weekend?

25:54.678 --> 25:55.763
[Yeon] Wait.

25:55.846 --> 25:57.556
[♪ light-hearted music playing]

26:00.142 --> 26:01.143
Your hand.

26:01.226 --> 26:03.353
[Yeon] You might slip
since you're wearing heels.

26:07.483 --> 26:08.942
It's fine, I can wipe them.

26:09.610 --> 26:10.611
Be careful.

26:13.655 --> 26:15.657
[♪ light-hearted music continues]

26:17.868 --> 26:19.119
[stammers]

26:19.203 --> 26:21.538
You really are considerate.

26:22.247 --> 26:24.500
You always look out for our family.

26:27.961 --> 26:29.922
Why did he cry, though?

26:31.632 --> 26:32.633
[♪ music ends]

26:35.636 --> 26:36.637
[cell phone vibrates]

26:37.346 --> 26:38.972
[Chan] How was your visit to your parents?

26:39.473 --> 26:40.724
[Hayeong] Hey.

26:40.808 --> 26:43.227
Whose message
is making you smile like that?

26:43.852 --> 26:45.145
What?

26:45.229 --> 26:47.940
What took you so long?
Weren't you looking for your phone?

26:48.023 --> 26:49.942
I was hungry, so I got some oxtail soup.

26:50.567 --> 26:52.111
[grunts] I'm so full.

26:52.194 --> 26:53.487
[chuckling] That's good.

26:53.570 --> 26:54.947
Hey, Hayeong.

26:55.739 --> 26:59.910
Did you ever tell Mr. Seonu about my past?

26:59.993 --> 27:02.955
Like how I was different before
or something like that?

27:03.038 --> 27:06.458
Like how you used to be
really bubbly and friendly?

27:06.542 --> 27:07.918
Something like that.

27:08.001 --> 27:09.545
Mmm? No, I didn't…

27:11.004 --> 27:12.881
[gasps] Wait, did I?

27:13.715 --> 27:15.968
[groans] I'm 29 now.

27:16.051 --> 27:17.261
My memory isn't so good…

27:18.595 --> 27:21.849
-But why do you ask?
-He spoke as if he knew me.

27:22.307 --> 27:23.308
Really?

27:24.476 --> 27:27.521
But are you two really close?

27:27.604 --> 27:29.731
Mr. Seonu, Ms. Song…

27:29.815 --> 27:30.941
You're so formal.

27:31.775 --> 27:33.735
Then what should I call him?

27:33.819 --> 27:35.404
You're the same age.

27:35.487 --> 27:37.114
Use your first names.

27:37.197 --> 27:39.867
You can just say, "Hey, Haran. Hey, Chan…"

27:42.452 --> 27:43.620
I should go shower.

27:43.704 --> 27:45.080
Why did you suddenly stop?

27:45.914 --> 27:46.999
Well…

27:48.125 --> 27:50.335
You used to call him Chan.

27:51.128 --> 27:54.423
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

27:55.716 --> 27:57.885
I just realized their names were similar.

27:58.760 --> 28:00.137
Oh…

28:00.220 --> 28:02.764
Right. I didn't think about that.

28:02.848 --> 28:04.892
[♪ emotional music playing]

28:04.975 --> 28:06.351
[mumbles]

28:07.352 --> 28:09.062
[mumbling] Make…

28:09.146 --> 28:12.774
MAKE HER HAPPY AGAIN, NO MATTER WHAT!

28:13.358 --> 28:14.359
[♪ music fades]

28:14.776 --> 28:17.446
[Haran] Their names… were similar.

28:18.238 --> 28:19.489
[sighs] All right…

28:21.992 --> 28:23.952
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

28:24.036 --> 28:25.037
[sighs]

28:25.621 --> 28:27.706
-[thuds loudly]
-[metallic clink echoes]

28:28.832 --> 28:30.292
What was that?

28:30.792 --> 28:33.670
EMPTY SPOT IN MEMORY - FOURTH

28:34.838 --> 28:37.007
A waste container…

28:37.883 --> 28:38.967
and that sound again.

28:41.011 --> 28:42.429
The lab…

28:42.512 --> 28:44.014
The sound of metal…

28:44.097 --> 28:45.349
The explosion.

28:45.432 --> 28:49.102
The missing gap
started with that sound, too.

28:52.773 --> 28:54.608
And the second memory

28:55.233 --> 28:56.443
had that sound as well.

28:57.945 --> 28:59.738
-[Sujin exclaims]
-[metallic clink]

28:59.821 --> 29:03.784
[Chan] And the third memory
had the same sound.

29:05.243 --> 29:07.079
Why did those missing memories

29:07.871 --> 29:10.040
start with the sound of her bracelet?

29:10.123 --> 29:12.042
[Hyeokchan] Sorry, Ran.
My professor's calling.

29:12.125 --> 29:13.210
I'll call you back later.

29:13.293 --> 29:14.628
Hey, Sujin. You're here?

29:15.128 --> 29:18.799
Why are they all connected to this person?

29:22.469 --> 29:25.263
SUJIN?

29:26.181 --> 29:27.724
Sujin?

29:30.018 --> 29:31.603
[metallic clink echoes]

29:35.691 --> 29:37.693
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

29:44.658 --> 29:46.243
This is Cha Sujin.

29:46.326 --> 29:47.911
I've arrived in Korea.

29:47.995 --> 29:49.997
I'll head to the hospital straight away.

29:50.747 --> 29:52.833
[metallic clink echoes]

29:55.293 --> 29:56.294
[♪ music ends]

29:56.795 --> 29:59.047
It's my fault for causing
the misunderstanding.

29:59.756 --> 30:00.924
I'm sorry.

30:02.342 --> 30:03.760
I'm sorry about everything.

30:04.678 --> 30:05.929
[taps]

30:09.266 --> 30:10.767
I'm sorry about everything.

30:11.393 --> 30:12.769
I'm sorry about everything…

30:19.026 --> 30:21.319
[Hadam] I'll give it to you. Text me.

30:21.820 --> 30:23.822
[♪ tense music playing]

30:28.702 --> 30:31.204
[groaning]

30:45.052 --> 30:46.053
[Changmo] Cha Yougyum?

30:47.971 --> 30:50.057
Hey, what are you doing here?

30:50.140 --> 30:51.141
[breathing shakily]

30:51.224 --> 30:53.852
[Yougyum singing heartbreaking ballad]

31:03.528 --> 31:05.530
[crying]

31:09.743 --> 31:11.495
What are you doing? Give it.

31:12.788 --> 31:14.790
[continues singing]

31:21.546 --> 31:24.591
[shatter echoes]

31:26.343 --> 31:27.552
[Hayeong] Are you okay?

31:28.386 --> 31:29.679
Oh?

31:29.763 --> 31:30.764
That's Mom's dish.

31:30.847 --> 31:32.349
Song Hadam.

31:32.432 --> 31:33.934
Don't you know we never use that?

31:34.017 --> 31:35.811
There are dozens of dishes. Why did you--

31:35.894 --> 31:38.313
Then why are you making a fuss
over one dish?

31:38.396 --> 31:40.899
Hey. Why are you talking like that?

31:40.982 --> 31:42.859
Don't you know what that dish is?

31:42.943 --> 31:44.152
-It's Mom's--
-I don't!

31:44.903 --> 31:45.946
I don't know.

31:46.029 --> 31:47.739
I'm the only one who doesn't know.

31:47.823 --> 31:50.450
I can hardly even remember
Mom and Dad's voices or faces,

31:50.534 --> 31:53.286
so how would I know
how special that stupid dish is?

31:53.370 --> 31:55.539
I want to remember, too.

31:55.622 --> 31:57.582
I want to miss them too,

31:58.250 --> 32:00.335
but I can't remember.

32:02.379 --> 32:07.175
Whenever you talk about Mom and Dad,
I feel like I don't belong.

32:08.009 --> 32:10.762
I feel like I'm the only one
who wasn't their daughter.

32:12.264 --> 32:14.891
-Hey…
-I was only six.

32:15.517 --> 32:16.726
I…

32:18.019 --> 32:19.479
I didn't know anything…

32:19.563 --> 32:21.064
[sighs softly]

32:21.148 --> 32:22.149
Hadam.

32:22.858 --> 32:23.900
We're sorry.

32:23.984 --> 32:25.569
[crying] I'm sorry, Hadam.

32:26.486 --> 32:28.488
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

32:30.615 --> 32:31.825
[Hadam] I'm going to school.

32:32.742 --> 32:34.119
I'm really sorry…

32:36.788 --> 32:37.998
I broke Mom's dish.

32:43.503 --> 32:44.671
[sighs]

32:45.755 --> 32:46.756
[sniffles]

32:48.216 --> 32:49.217
[sighs]

32:49.801 --> 32:53.221
You said you have a meeting.
Go get ready. I'll clean this.

32:53.763 --> 32:54.931
[sighs]

32:55.724 --> 32:56.808
Okay, thanks.

32:57.434 --> 32:59.436
We'll talk to Hadam when she comes home.

33:00.437 --> 33:02.272
[dish clinking]

33:11.239 --> 33:12.365
Hey, Hadam.

33:15.535 --> 33:17.579
Let me see your hand. Where is it?

33:18.580 --> 33:19.831
[sighs] Gosh.

33:21.499 --> 33:22.500
[♪ music ends]

33:25.962 --> 33:28.089
I just got this at a convenience store.

33:28.173 --> 33:29.466
It's just a temporary fix,

33:29.549 --> 33:32.886
so go to the nurse's office, okay?

33:34.012 --> 33:36.473
But what do we do

33:37.474 --> 33:38.683
about Mom's dish?

33:39.267 --> 33:41.019
That dish isn't the problem.

33:41.102 --> 33:43.104
You hurt your hand
when the CSAT is coming up.

33:43.772 --> 33:45.398
I'm ambidextrous.

33:46.650 --> 33:48.652
You are? Since when?

33:48.735 --> 33:50.528
I practiced using my left hand

33:50.612 --> 33:52.656
because my hand hurt
when I studied too long.

33:52.739 --> 33:54.282
But I was a natural at it.

33:54.950 --> 33:56.201
Our baby sister.

33:56.952 --> 33:58.245
You take after Mom.

33:59.871 --> 34:00.872
Mom?

34:01.957 --> 34:03.541
Mom was ambidextrous.

34:04.417 --> 34:06.461
[exclaims] We wondered
where her genes went.

34:06.544 --> 34:08.463
I guess they all went to you.

34:08.964 --> 34:10.799
[♪ pleasant music playing]

34:10.882 --> 34:14.886
Did you want to find out
what she meant by feeling sparkly?

34:15.887 --> 34:17.180
Is that why you took it out?

34:17.806 --> 34:18.807
Huh?

34:18.890 --> 34:23.436
Didn't you want to eat sweets from it
and feel better?

34:27.315 --> 34:28.441
Hadam.

34:28.525 --> 34:31.236
Let's talk more about Mom and Dad
from now on.

34:32.445 --> 34:37.033
I was actually worried
we'd forget about them when time passed.

34:37.117 --> 34:40.704
But I guess we can tell
our smart baby sister about them

34:40.787 --> 34:42.205
as a backup file.

34:43.373 --> 34:46.293
I do have a good memory.

34:46.376 --> 34:47.669
[both chuckle]

34:47.752 --> 34:51.089
How long are you going to follow me?

34:52.549 --> 34:55.760
I'm escorting you properly today,

34:56.219 --> 34:57.387
all the way to school.

34:58.513 --> 35:03.101
Aren't you the least bit aware
of your current condition?

35:04.311 --> 35:06.813
-Are you embarrassed of me?
-A bit.

35:07.606 --> 35:08.773
Hadam!

35:08.857 --> 35:10.358
[Hadam] Oh? It's Yeongju.

35:10.442 --> 35:11.651
Bye.

35:11.735 --> 35:12.861
Jeong Yeongju!

35:13.653 --> 35:15.322
Go to the nurse's office!

35:16.406 --> 35:18.825
You'll catch a cold. Go home.

35:19.909 --> 35:21.536
Bye! [giggles]

35:31.546 --> 35:32.631
[sighs]

35:32.714 --> 35:33.715
[♪ music ends]

35:34.424 --> 35:36.843
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

35:39.346 --> 35:42.182
[toy] Let's go on a walk.

35:42.265 --> 35:44.351
-[sighs] Genius.
-[toy] Let's go on a walk.

35:44.434 --> 35:46.311
You seem to be abusing that.

35:46.394 --> 35:50.607
-And you're such a chatterbox.
-[whimpers]

35:50.690 --> 35:51.900
Watch your mouth, okay?

35:52.275 --> 35:53.276
[grunts]

35:53.360 --> 35:55.945
-[toy] Let's play.
-Okay. [chuckles]

35:56.571 --> 35:57.572
Let's go on a walk.

35:57.656 --> 35:59.783
Mr. Park, I'll go on a run with Genius.

35:59.866 --> 36:01.242
Don't you have a meeting?

36:01.326 --> 36:02.661
I still have some time.

36:02.744 --> 36:03.953
Right.

36:04.037 --> 36:07.248
Something arrived from the US
while you were away.

36:07.332 --> 36:09.959
I forgot about it.
It's in the counter cabinet.

36:10.043 --> 36:11.044
Ah.

36:18.134 --> 36:20.136
[♪ pensive music playing]

36:22.597 --> 36:23.598
[cell phone buzzes]

36:27.936 --> 36:28.937
Mmm?

36:33.525 --> 36:34.526
Hello?

36:35.985 --> 36:37.487
What was that message?

36:38.071 --> 36:39.656
Why is it a secret from Ms. Song?

36:42.325 --> 36:43.326
Ah.

36:44.035 --> 36:46.538
Okay, I'll keep it a secret. All right.

36:48.915 --> 36:50.458
What did you receive?

36:50.542 --> 36:53.211
[chuckles awkwardly] It's nothing special.

36:53.294 --> 36:54.504
[Manjae chuckles]

36:55.547 --> 36:57.716
I'll clean up. Go. He's so eager to leave.

36:57.799 --> 36:59.092
[both chuckle]

36:59.175 --> 37:01.010
-Genius, let's go. Come on.
-Go on.

37:01.886 --> 37:03.763
[Chan] Let's go, Genius.

37:03.847 --> 37:05.056
-Let's run!
-[chuckles]

37:05.807 --> 37:06.808
[grunts]

37:08.601 --> 37:10.019
[humming]

37:10.103 --> 37:11.271
[exclaims softly]

37:15.650 --> 37:16.651
What is this?

37:17.235 --> 37:20.155
[in English] "Newbury Street, Boston…"

37:20.989 --> 37:22.615
[in Korean] What was the package?

37:23.658 --> 37:24.993
-[patron 1] Hello, Mr. Park.
-Oh!

37:25.076 --> 37:27.203
-[patron 2] Hello.
-Welcome. Come in.

37:32.083 --> 37:34.753
You mean there will be
more parts on Korea?

37:34.836 --> 37:38.381
Yes, the interim feedback
was really positive.

37:38.465 --> 37:41.217
The response to Won's outfit
was incredible.

37:41.301 --> 37:45.889
The cloud motif, Korean color palette,
dancheong, and the hanbok panel.

37:45.972 --> 37:51.060
Wow. Everyone was impressed
by the details that represented Korea.

37:51.144 --> 37:56.149
The most Korean things
are what end up being popular worldwide!

37:56.733 --> 38:01.279
So we'd like to request another outfit
once we get the revised script,

38:02.113 --> 38:04.282
if that's okay with you…

38:04.365 --> 38:07.035
Don't be silly. Of course, that's okay.

38:07.827 --> 38:10.205
If it will help with the project,
anything's fine.

38:12.165 --> 38:13.583
-Thank you.
-[Ben] Thank you.

38:14.125 --> 38:16.377
Right. We just have to push
straight ahead now.

38:16.461 --> 38:18.505
Let's pick up the pace again.

38:18.588 --> 38:20.340
How about a round of applause?

38:20.423 --> 38:22.842
Everybody, clap!

38:22.926 --> 38:24.677
[applause]

38:32.519 --> 38:35.188
Plans? Is it about work?

38:36.105 --> 38:37.190
[Chan] Mmm…

38:37.273 --> 38:39.108
I think it's a secret.

38:46.407 --> 38:49.244
There should at least be
one pen that you like.

38:51.329 --> 38:53.498
I guess she didn't find
any that she liked.

38:53.998 --> 38:54.999
What?

38:55.083 --> 38:56.125
It's nothing. [chuckles softly]

38:56.209 --> 38:57.418
[elevator dings]

38:57.502 --> 38:58.878
Bye, then.

39:00.380 --> 39:01.506
Bye.

39:03.091 --> 39:04.551
See you later. I'll text you.

39:09.347 --> 39:11.891
Who is he meeting, though?

39:12.684 --> 39:15.520
[Nana] Then are your parents
in LA as well?

39:15.603 --> 39:16.813
[♪ traditional Korean music plays]

39:16.896 --> 39:19.440
Oh… No. [inhales sharply]

39:19.983 --> 39:22.151
My mother passed away when I was nine.

39:22.235 --> 39:26.197
My father's probably teaching in Daejeon.

39:26.281 --> 39:27.824
We don't really keep in touch.

39:28.867 --> 39:29.868
Well…

39:30.368 --> 39:34.664
Every family has its own issues.

39:35.540 --> 39:37.125
Go on and eat.

39:37.208 --> 39:38.585
Thank you.

39:38.668 --> 39:39.836
Right.

39:39.919 --> 39:43.006
Will you stay in LA again
once the collaboration is over?

39:43.089 --> 39:44.173
[♪ amusing music playing]

39:44.257 --> 39:47.010
Yes, I believe so. But why do you ask?

39:48.094 --> 39:50.555
Should I establish a branch in LA
and send her there?

39:51.598 --> 39:52.765
Excuse me?

39:52.849 --> 39:55.393
Ah. I was just talking to myself.

39:55.476 --> 39:59.105
-[chuckles awkwardly]
-But why aren't you eating? Hmm?

39:59.188 --> 40:02.609
I wanted to treat you to something
after all that trouble at headquarters.

40:02.692 --> 40:03.735
Eat up.

40:03.818 --> 40:07.697
Why did you only ask for me?
Ben went through a lot, too.

40:07.780 --> 40:09.782
-Who?
-You know, with the…

40:10.366 --> 40:13.536
Oh… Producer Ben?

40:13.620 --> 40:14.954
Well,

40:15.038 --> 40:18.124
I'm sure his in-laws
will take good care of him.

40:18.207 --> 40:21.419
Just think of this as a meal
from your in-laws.

40:21.502 --> 40:23.796
-[Nana chuckles]
-In-laws?

40:24.672 --> 40:27.926
-I'm just saying…
-[♪ music fades]

40:28.009 --> 40:30.053
[groans] Darn it. I can't do this.

40:32.055 --> 40:33.264
I'm sorry.

40:33.348 --> 40:35.850
Beating around the bush
isn't really my style,

40:35.934 --> 40:37.435
so let me be blunt.

40:37.518 --> 40:39.228
Oh. Sure, be blunt…

40:39.854 --> 40:41.731
I mean, feel free to say what you want.

40:43.441 --> 40:46.486
How much do you know about Haran's past?

40:47.487 --> 40:48.780
Quite a lot.

40:50.239 --> 40:52.700
Did you hear about her losing her parents?

40:54.243 --> 40:55.244
I heard.

40:55.328 --> 40:58.539
And losing her boyfriend seven years ago?

41:01.960 --> 41:03.336
I know that, too.

41:06.673 --> 41:08.049
Even after losing her parents,

41:09.050 --> 41:11.469
she stayed strong,

41:12.387 --> 41:15.556
but that incident left Haran
trapped in winter,

41:16.432 --> 41:18.643
just like you said.

41:19.310 --> 41:20.436
[♪ dramatic music playing]

41:20.520 --> 41:21.980
Haran's not eating.

41:22.063 --> 41:23.398
Again?

41:23.481 --> 41:26.734
She's not eating or sleeping.

41:26.818 --> 41:28.319
She'll die at this rate, Grandma.

41:29.779 --> 41:32.615
[Nana] She no longer smiled
or showed any expressions…

41:32.699 --> 41:35.410
-Eat a sausage, Hadam.
-…even in front of her sisters,

41:35.493 --> 41:37.912
and even in front of me,
when we used to be like friends.

41:37.996 --> 41:39.706
[Haran] Just don't go.

41:39.789 --> 41:42.166
What if something happens to you outside?

41:42.250 --> 41:45.294
It happened to Mom and Dad.
So don't go, okay?

41:46.212 --> 41:49.507
It's okay.
Haran, it's all right. It's okay.

41:49.590 --> 41:52.010
If I let her stay buried
in all that anxiety,

41:52.593 --> 41:54.262
I felt like I would lose her.

41:59.142 --> 42:00.268
Come out.

42:00.351 --> 42:01.352
I'm not eating.

42:02.437 --> 42:03.813
Just leave me alone.

42:03.896 --> 42:05.481
Get up. Right now.

42:05.565 --> 42:09.569
I knew I had to do whatever I could
to pull her out.

42:10.570 --> 42:12.113
You're working here from now on.

42:12.196 --> 42:14.282
I'll give you a month
to organize the storage room.

42:14.365 --> 42:16.451
Why are you doing this?

42:17.160 --> 42:19.162
I don't want to. I'm leaving.

42:19.787 --> 42:20.788
That's an order.

42:20.872 --> 42:23.249
If you want to keep sleeping
under my roof,

42:23.875 --> 42:25.001
do as I say.

42:25.835 --> 42:29.297
I had to grow cold,
and I had to stay strong.

42:29.380 --> 42:32.759
I had to save her first.

42:33.801 --> 42:35.136
[door slams]

42:35.636 --> 42:36.637
[sighs]

42:42.560 --> 42:43.561
[♪ music fades]

42:45.063 --> 42:46.230
[lightbulb buzzing]

42:49.358 --> 42:50.359
[sighs]

42:54.655 --> 42:56.616
-[buttons clatter]
-[sighs]

42:56.699 --> 42:58.701
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

43:12.256 --> 43:13.549
Come out.

43:18.763 --> 43:21.057
[Nana] She could hardly move an inch,

43:21.140 --> 43:24.435
but she finally started moving
little by little,

43:24.519 --> 43:26.187
and her eyes started shining.

43:29.107 --> 43:30.191
[sighs wearily]

43:37.448 --> 43:40.535
[Nana] She was living again,
little by little.

43:50.044 --> 43:51.587
She's alive now.

43:56.008 --> 43:58.010
[♪ uplifting music playing]

44:02.598 --> 44:04.851
Come to work on the third floor
starting tomorrow.

44:05.685 --> 44:10.398
You'll be the rookie assistant
for Design Team 1, 2, and 3.

44:12.817 --> 44:16.070
I was relieved at the fact
that she held on once more

44:16.154 --> 44:17.947
without crumbling down.

44:18.030 --> 44:20.658
But then, she changed.

44:20.741 --> 44:23.536
-This is an apology for taking a leave.
-[Pureum] Thank you.

44:23.619 --> 44:25.538
[Nana] She started smiling again recently.

44:26.622 --> 44:29.417
I know I met a great person.

44:29.500 --> 44:31.252
I feel grateful.

44:32.253 --> 44:33.880
[Nana] She learned how to cry again, too.

44:38.634 --> 44:39.760
Mr. Seonu.

44:42.180 --> 44:43.431
Why would you…

44:43.890 --> 44:44.891
Thank you.

44:45.558 --> 44:47.727
I wanted to speak to you today

44:47.810 --> 44:50.229
as Haran's grandmother,
not the head of the atelier.

44:51.189 --> 44:54.775
Thank you so much for letting me see Haran

44:54.859 --> 44:58.029
crying and laughing again.

44:59.488 --> 45:01.199
[stammers] No, I…

45:01.949 --> 45:03.034
I didn't do anything…

45:03.117 --> 45:04.869
They say that if it's fate,

45:04.952 --> 45:07.330
you'll meet
no matter how far apart you are.

45:07.413 --> 45:08.748
You came all the way here.

45:08.831 --> 45:11.125
I don't think
you were meant to just work here.

45:11.209 --> 45:12.543
[♪ music ends]

45:12.627 --> 45:13.669
Thanks to you,

45:14.587 --> 45:16.172
I'll be able to leave in peace.

45:17.840 --> 45:19.300
Are you going somewhere?

45:20.301 --> 45:21.302
Well,

45:22.720 --> 45:26.265
I'm planning to stay in France
after I retire.

45:26.349 --> 45:27.975
If you stay by Haran's side,

45:28.059 --> 45:30.978
I won't be that worried about her.

45:31.062 --> 45:32.772
Ah. [sighs]

45:34.774 --> 45:37.985
[inhales sharply] But, Ms. Kim,

45:39.237 --> 45:41.948
I may not be as good for her

45:43.449 --> 45:47.078
as you believe.

45:47.620 --> 45:49.622
[♪ suspenseful music plays]

45:54.710 --> 45:57.421
My heart is throbbing,

45:58.631 --> 46:00.341
and tears keep flowing.

46:01.092 --> 46:02.093
My heart

46:03.261 --> 46:04.929
hurts more than my foot.

46:06.055 --> 46:07.765
Do you think it's serious?

46:07.848 --> 46:11.310
Cut the drama and go to a bigger hospital.

46:11.394 --> 46:12.979
I can't treat that properly here.

46:13.062 --> 46:15.606
I'm sure it's just because
I trained hard these days.

46:16.148 --> 46:17.775
Just give me something for the bruise.

46:17.858 --> 46:19.443
[♪ whimsical music playing]

46:19.527 --> 46:20.528
[sighs]

46:25.449 --> 46:26.784
Can you move aside?

46:26.867 --> 46:28.536
Huh? Oh…

46:28.619 --> 46:29.620
[♪ music fades]

46:38.796 --> 46:40.131
Can I help you with anything?

46:40.214 --> 46:42.675
Why did Yougyum come here?

46:43.259 --> 46:44.510
Is he hurt?

46:44.593 --> 46:45.803
That's personal information.

46:45.886 --> 46:47.680
-[doctor chuckles]
-[♪ music continues]

46:48.597 --> 46:51.392
[sighs] Is she sick or something?

46:52.226 --> 46:53.227
[sighs]

46:54.020 --> 46:56.314
She has to stay healthy.

47:01.068 --> 47:02.069
[♪ music ends]

47:02.903 --> 47:04.864
-Mmm.
-[Haran gasps]

47:04.947 --> 47:06.657
Hey, you came back.

47:06.741 --> 47:11.120
I finished my first appointment,
so I'm here for the next one with you.

47:11.829 --> 47:12.830
[Chan chuckles]

47:13.664 --> 47:16.250
Seriously, what are we doing here?

47:16.334 --> 47:17.335
You'll see.

47:18.419 --> 47:21.505
KIM SEON POTTERY EXHIBITION

47:22.256 --> 47:23.716
Pottery exhibition?

47:24.967 --> 47:26.093
No way.

47:26.177 --> 47:28.137
-[Chan's grandma] Oh. You're here.
-Grandma!

47:30.139 --> 47:32.850
-Goodness. [exclaims excitedly]
-[♪ pleasant music playing]

47:32.933 --> 47:34.894
-[Chan's grandma] I missed you.
-I feel neglected lately.

47:34.977 --> 47:36.103
-[Chan's grandma] How are you?
-It's okay.

47:36.187 --> 47:37.188
Have you been well?

47:37.855 --> 47:39.982
You should have told me
we were seeing her.

47:40.066 --> 47:41.901
It's not my fault. She told me not to.

47:42.777 --> 47:44.653
If I'd known, I would've gotten flowers--

47:44.737 --> 47:46.864
That's why I told him to keep it secret.

47:46.947 --> 47:51.035
And why would I need flowers
when such a precious guest is here?

47:51.786 --> 47:52.995
Are you two dating?

47:53.704 --> 47:55.122
You little brat.

47:55.206 --> 47:57.750
You should've told me
you were going to the States.

47:57.833 --> 48:00.544
-I was worried when I couldn't reach you.
-I told you.

48:00.628 --> 48:03.255
-I suddenly had to go--
-Still, you should have told her.

48:03.339 --> 48:04.340
Right?

48:04.423 --> 48:06.133
Wow. You're teaming up on me?

48:06.217 --> 48:07.635
That's so mean. I'm leaving.

48:07.718 --> 48:10.638
Come and look around.
And get the cup you made last time.

48:10.721 --> 48:12.640
It looks so beautiful.

48:12.723 --> 48:15.893
[Haran] Really? I'm so excited.
[exclaims excitedly]

48:15.976 --> 48:17.812
[Chan's grandma]
My hands look pretty, don't they?

48:17.895 --> 48:20.106
-No one's coming for me? [scoffs]
-[♪ music ends]

48:20.189 --> 48:21.607
I want to be doted on, too!

48:35.579 --> 48:37.498
Oh. This one looks a bit different.

48:37.581 --> 48:41.127
The lines seem pretty rough,
but it's so cool.

48:41.210 --> 48:44.088
The lines are where I mended them.

48:44.672 --> 48:47.508
I put together the shattered pieces.

48:48.008 --> 48:49.844
You can put shattered pieces together?

48:49.927 --> 48:51.303
[Chan's grandma]
You know lacquer trees, right?

48:51.387 --> 48:53.681
The sap acts as a natural adhesive.

48:54.265 --> 48:57.601
Once I attach the pieces
and let them dry carefully…

48:57.685 --> 49:01.063
Then they become a new art piece.

49:02.898 --> 49:07.027
They shatter, get hurt, then heal,

49:07.653 --> 49:09.530
and in the process, they gain depth.

49:10.781 --> 49:12.992
It's similar to people, right?

49:14.702 --> 49:16.370
[Chan's grandma chuckles]

49:16.454 --> 49:20.541
Oh… Would it be possible
to restore a broken plate?

49:20.624 --> 49:24.044
It's a dish my mom treasured,
but they don't sell it anymore.

49:24.128 --> 49:27.381
Bring it over sometime.
I'll do my best to restore it.

49:27.840 --> 49:29.508
-[sighs in relief]
-[woman] Ms. Kim.

49:29.592 --> 49:31.969
[exclaims] You're here. Hang on.

49:32.553 --> 49:33.804
Look around.

49:33.888 --> 49:35.890
[women exclaim, lively chatter]

49:36.557 --> 49:38.476
We shouldn't meet like this anymore.

49:38.559 --> 49:39.768
I just get lonely.

49:39.852 --> 49:41.061
[chuckles]

49:41.145 --> 49:44.440
Shouldn't you go and greet them?
They seem like her friends.

49:44.523 --> 49:46.358
Chan, come and say hi.

49:46.442 --> 49:47.818
Okay.

49:47.902 --> 49:49.403
I'll be back soon.

49:52.364 --> 49:55.451
Oh. The kid who visited during vacation?

49:55.534 --> 49:58.621
-Yes.
-You've gotten so handsome!

49:58.704 --> 50:01.373
Thank you.
I turned out pretty well, didn't I?

50:01.457 --> 50:04.043
Oh my. Look how cheeky he's gotten.

50:04.126 --> 50:05.544
[grandmas chuckle]

50:05.628 --> 50:07.338
[Hayeong] You used to call him Chan.

50:07.421 --> 50:10.257
Your old boyfriend, Hyeokchan.

50:11.008 --> 50:12.384
Seonu Chan?

50:14.345 --> 50:15.471
Seonu…

50:16.305 --> 50:17.348
Chan.

50:17.848 --> 50:19.683
[♪ mellow music plays]

50:21.894 --> 50:23.354
[Chan's grandma] He's shameless, like me.

50:23.437 --> 50:25.231
[all laugh]

50:30.986 --> 50:32.988
Oh? There's no one here.

50:33.072 --> 50:34.615
Everyone went home.

50:34.698 --> 50:36.116
Is Hayeong not here?

50:36.200 --> 50:38.536
We were going to discuss
the new material today.

50:38.619 --> 50:41.330
She was feeble all day,
unlike her usual self,

50:41.413 --> 50:42.790
and went home early.

50:42.873 --> 50:44.291
Try calling her.

50:44.375 --> 50:45.376
Bye, then.

50:50.965 --> 50:52.174
[line connects, rings]

50:52.258 --> 50:53.926
Ms. Song.

50:54.009 --> 50:55.094
[man] Hello?

50:55.177 --> 50:56.929
Are you a friend of hers?

50:58.138 --> 51:00.933
She's been drinking and sleeping nonstop.

51:01.016 --> 51:02.768
You should come and take her home.

51:03.602 --> 51:05.604
[♪ upbeat music playing over speakers]

51:15.781 --> 51:16.782
Ah. [laughs]

51:17.408 --> 51:19.493
Good morning.

51:20.077 --> 51:21.579
When did I come to work, though?

51:21.662 --> 51:23.831
You got off work. This is a wine bar.

51:23.914 --> 51:25.416
I'll take you home.

51:25.499 --> 51:28.377
What? To where? Home?

51:28.460 --> 51:30.588
[groans] No, I can't.

51:31.589 --> 51:33.757
I can't face Hadam.

51:36.510 --> 51:40.097
I should have told her more
about Mom and Dad.

51:41.056 --> 51:43.392
I should have known how she felt.

51:44.435 --> 51:46.895
I should have known

51:47.688 --> 51:49.732
so no one would get hurt.

51:51.483 --> 51:55.154
Hadam was only six at the time.

51:55.237 --> 51:59.158
But she was in the car with Mom and Dad

51:59.950 --> 52:01.368
during…

52:02.244 --> 52:04.038
the accident…

52:05.706 --> 52:07.708
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

52:17.635 --> 52:18.761
It's cold.

52:43.786 --> 52:44.787
[♪ music fades]

52:50.584 --> 52:52.127
[♪ whimsical music playing]

52:56.256 --> 52:59.677
It's just that you were crying…

53:00.177 --> 53:03.222
[exclaims] It's just drool.

53:03.931 --> 53:06.934
[stutters] Let's go.

53:07.017 --> 53:08.894
-All right.
-[Hayeong clears throat]

53:11.063 --> 53:12.231
The GPS…

53:14.942 --> 53:16.402
Wait.

53:16.485 --> 53:17.695
Seongsu-dong?

53:17.778 --> 53:18.779
[♪ music fades]

53:25.536 --> 53:26.954
Was I mistaken?

53:28.080 --> 53:31.667
Did you go to Seongsu-dong last Thursday?

53:32.710 --> 53:34.336
You were with Grandma, right?

53:35.003 --> 53:37.005
-No. I'll start the car.
-Wait.

53:37.089 --> 53:38.924
I saw Grandma that day.

53:39.007 --> 53:41.218
I'm sure I saw her crying.

53:42.094 --> 53:43.929
She was crying?

53:44.012 --> 53:45.806
So you did go to Seongsu-dong, right?

53:47.808 --> 53:49.518
[sighs] That woke me right up.

53:51.854 --> 53:52.980
Is something going on?

53:54.565 --> 53:55.941
What is it?

53:56.024 --> 53:58.360
I'm sorry, but just let this go for now.

53:59.695 --> 54:00.863
Please.

54:10.289 --> 54:12.291
[♪ somber music playing]

54:26.054 --> 54:28.348
MISSING ELDERLY WITH DEMENTIA

54:28.432 --> 54:29.433
[♪ music fades]

54:33.479 --> 54:35.898
You can't stop looking at it.
Are you that impressed?

54:35.981 --> 54:37.691
Are you sure I really made this?

54:37.775 --> 54:39.693
Did you make it again
because it was a mess?

54:39.777 --> 54:41.612
-Of course not.
-[both laugh]

54:42.321 --> 54:46.200
I'd love to have dinner with you,
but I'm meeting the people who helped me.

54:46.283 --> 54:49.578
I'll stay in Seoul for a few days,
so let's have a meal sometime.

54:49.661 --> 54:51.705
And bring your mother's dish then.

54:51.788 --> 54:53.081
All right.

54:53.165 --> 54:55.459
Her mother's dish? What do you mean?

54:55.542 --> 54:57.711
-Why are you curious about everything?
-[groans]

54:57.794 --> 55:00.130
Grandma, don't do that in front of her.

55:00.214 --> 55:01.548
-[Chan groans]
-Your cheeks are so squishy.

55:01.632 --> 55:02.633
[Haran and Chan's grandma chuckle]

55:05.260 --> 55:06.595
The weather's so nice.

55:07.179 --> 55:08.347
How about dinner--

55:08.430 --> 55:10.224
Sorry, but you should go home first.

55:10.933 --> 55:12.935
-I'll see you later.
-Where are you going?

55:13.477 --> 55:14.728
Ms. Song!

55:16.730 --> 55:19.483
Being overly polite
will hurt her feelings.

55:19.566 --> 55:22.194
But I should at least give her
some hand lotion.

55:23.862 --> 55:24.863
Huh?

55:29.618 --> 55:31.203
Oh? Did she leave?

55:32.704 --> 55:33.705
Hang on.

55:37.251 --> 55:39.044
-She's not here?
-Did she leave?

55:39.127 --> 55:40.462
We can come back…

55:40.546 --> 55:41.547
[exclaims softly]

55:42.923 --> 55:43.924
Hmm?

55:44.007 --> 55:46.009
[♪ tense music playing]

55:50.430 --> 55:52.099
[young Chan] Dad. Dad!

55:52.182 --> 55:54.226
[Chan's dad] What more do I have to do
to make you stop?

55:59.231 --> 56:00.566
Let's just go.

56:00.649 --> 56:03.026
-Wait, I…
-[Chan's dad] Chan.

56:07.406 --> 56:09.408
[chuckles awkwardly] You're back.

56:10.075 --> 56:13.036
He had business nearby

56:13.120 --> 56:16.790
and dropped by to greet me
when he saw the sign.

56:17.791 --> 56:19.293
[Chan's dad inhales sharply, hesitates]

56:20.043 --> 56:21.169
It's been a while.

56:23.463 --> 56:26.341
There was
an international conference nearby.

56:26.425 --> 56:27.426
Your school…

56:28.093 --> 56:32.264
No, your former school
and some other schools--

56:32.347 --> 56:33.932
That's enough.

56:34.016 --> 56:35.434
I'm not even curious.

56:37.144 --> 56:38.895
-Let's go.
-How are you?

56:39.563 --> 56:41.648
How is your condition these days?

56:45.527 --> 56:48.405
[door opens, closes]

56:50.616 --> 56:51.742
Are you going somewhere?

56:55.245 --> 56:56.580
Why are you taking your passport?

56:57.414 --> 56:59.041
I don't want to stay in Korea.

56:59.625 --> 57:01.376
You made a good decision.

57:02.502 --> 57:06.256
You received enough treatment,
so you can return to school--

57:06.340 --> 57:07.758
I'm not…

57:08.759 --> 57:10.010
going back to school.

57:10.093 --> 57:11.386
I'm not studying anymore.

57:12.888 --> 57:15.057
What? You've already wasted so much time.

57:16.058 --> 57:19.478
Are you going to give up everything
just because of some accident?

57:19.978 --> 57:23.440
Stop acting like a child
and be reasonable.

57:23.523 --> 57:26.860
You should finish your master's
and move on to a PhD program…

57:27.486 --> 57:28.820
Do you not see me?

57:30.405 --> 57:34.201
I'm covered in burn scars,
and I can't hear on one side.

57:35.160 --> 57:37.579
-You call that "some accident"?
-It's in the past.

57:38.080 --> 57:39.623
Blaming it won't change anything.

57:39.706 --> 57:42.125
Enough with the pathetic self-pity!

57:43.043 --> 57:44.044
[scoffs lightly]

57:45.462 --> 57:46.797
[sighs]

57:46.880 --> 57:47.964
I get it now.

57:48.799 --> 57:52.219
This is why she left you.
It was because of you.

57:52.302 --> 57:54.054
She didn't just leave,

57:54.888 --> 57:56.306
you made her leave!

57:56.390 --> 57:58.141
I'll leave too.

57:58.225 --> 57:59.935
I'll live my own life,

58:00.477 --> 58:04.022
so just think
that your stupid, obedient son…

58:04.106 --> 58:05.107
[sighs]

58:06.817 --> 58:07.943
died…

58:09.152 --> 58:11.071
in that explosion.

58:12.739 --> 58:13.740
[♪ music ends]

58:14.324 --> 58:15.534
[sighs]

58:18.745 --> 58:19.996
Why are you acting like this?

58:20.080 --> 58:22.457
You never worried about me before.

58:22.541 --> 58:24.584
[♪ somber music playing]

58:25.210 --> 58:27.045
I saw you here earlier,

58:27.754 --> 58:31.550
so I left,
in case you'd feel uncomfortable.

58:33.009 --> 58:34.886
I didn't know you'd come back.

58:34.970 --> 58:36.054
You're right.

58:36.680 --> 58:38.265
I do feel uncomfortable.

58:38.348 --> 58:41.810
So if you ever see me anywhere again,

58:42.352 --> 58:43.353
don't even say hi.

58:43.437 --> 58:45.147
Chan, don't do this!

58:45.230 --> 58:47.733
Are you going to keep acting
like you're strangers?

58:47.816 --> 58:49.735
Since you've met… Hmm?

58:50.527 --> 58:52.195
Give her the flowers. I'm leaving.

58:53.989 --> 58:55.615
-Chan, let's talk--
-Stop!

58:55.699 --> 58:57.242
[Chan's grandma screams]

58:57.325 --> 58:58.618
[gasps]

58:58.702 --> 59:00.287
[Chan breathing heavily]

59:01.580 --> 59:02.873
[exhales heavily]

59:02.956 --> 59:05.959
[grunts angrily]

59:07.627 --> 59:09.629
[breath trembling]

59:11.757 --> 59:13.049
Chan! Don't. Stop.

59:13.133 --> 59:14.926
Let him go! Let go of him!

59:15.010 --> 59:16.094
Let him go.

59:16.178 --> 59:17.596
Don't do this!

59:17.679 --> 59:19.973
Chan, let him go!

59:20.056 --> 59:23.101
Go. Everyone, just go!

59:31.443 --> 59:32.903
[sighs wearily]

59:34.404 --> 59:36.239
Oh, dear. Let me see.

59:36.865 --> 59:38.158
Oh, no.

59:38.617 --> 59:39.618
I'm sorry.

59:39.701 --> 59:42.913
[breathes heavily] It's okay.
I didn't even notice. I'm really fine.

59:43.955 --> 59:46.875
Grandma, take care of her for me.

59:48.543 --> 59:50.003
Wait…

59:51.838 --> 59:53.131
He won't be able…

59:54.382 --> 59:56.176
to face you right now.

59:58.303 --> 59:59.971
[sighs heavily]

01:00:00.764 --> 01:00:01.973
[♪ music continues]

01:00:02.057 --> 01:00:03.391
[sighs wearily]

01:00:14.444 --> 01:00:16.696
Darn it…

01:00:25.455 --> 01:00:26.456
[♪ music fades]

01:00:27.582 --> 01:00:29.251
[Chan's grandma sighs]

01:00:29.334 --> 01:00:31.878
I'll be able to fix the shattered pottery,

01:00:33.380 --> 01:00:36.424
but I can't do anything
about their relationship.

01:00:37.425 --> 01:00:39.886
They've had a deep rift for a long time.

01:00:41.388 --> 01:00:43.390
[cell phone vibrating]

01:00:44.391 --> 01:00:45.976
You can take it.

01:00:46.059 --> 01:00:47.727
Sorry, hang on.

01:00:48.353 --> 01:00:49.688
Yes, Director.

01:00:50.689 --> 01:00:51.690
Yes.

01:00:51.773 --> 01:00:53.400
Of course.

01:01:02.242 --> 01:01:05.036
PROFESSOR SUNWOO SEOK

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:07.289
[Haran] "Science University"?

01:01:08.081 --> 01:01:09.541
[♪ pensive music playing]

01:01:09.624 --> 01:01:10.917
[Chan] From the smell,

01:01:11.001 --> 01:01:13.336
it seemed like
diluted sodium hypochlorite solution.

01:01:13.420 --> 01:01:16.089
Because of the diffraction of sunlight,
the cloud particles…

01:01:16.590 --> 01:01:18.049
Petrichor.

01:01:18.675 --> 01:01:20.760
[Seok] Your former school
and some other schools…

01:01:20.844 --> 01:01:22.429
[officer] I guess
you majored in that field.

01:01:22.512 --> 01:01:24.472
[Haran] It seems like
you majored in engineering.

01:01:24.556 --> 01:01:26.892
[Ben] He never tells me
what he did before entering CalArts.

01:01:26.975 --> 01:01:28.685
I lived like a corpse.

01:01:38.945 --> 01:01:40.030
[♪ music fades]

01:01:40.113 --> 01:01:41.114
[knock on door]

01:01:42.115 --> 01:01:44.492
Laundry…

01:01:44.576 --> 01:01:45.827
Is there any laundry?

01:01:47.203 --> 01:01:48.330
[object clatters]

01:01:50.707 --> 01:01:51.833
[grunts]

01:01:55.795 --> 01:01:57.923
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:01:59.549 --> 01:02:02.010
What happened to the pen you always use?

01:02:02.093 --> 01:02:03.970
I lost it, and I never found it.

01:02:04.054 --> 01:02:05.555
I'll just use a new one now.

01:02:06.431 --> 01:02:07.766
[Chan] It's nothing special.

01:02:08.975 --> 01:02:09.976
Wait.

01:02:10.685 --> 01:02:12.729
Why is this pen here?

01:02:13.271 --> 01:02:14.272
[♪ music fades]

01:02:18.526 --> 01:02:20.070
Huh? Genius.

01:02:21.196 --> 01:02:22.197
[sighs]

01:02:25.450 --> 01:02:26.952
Mr. Seonu.

01:02:27.827 --> 01:02:29.371
Oh? You're in here.

01:02:29.454 --> 01:02:31.623
Yes, I was collecting laundry.

01:02:31.706 --> 01:02:34.084
But why did you come upstairs?

01:02:34.167 --> 01:02:36.127
Sorry, I came without asking.

01:02:36.211 --> 01:02:39.172
I just wanted to see Mr. Seonu.
I have something to give him.

01:02:39.255 --> 01:02:41.174
He hasn't come home yet.

01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:42.759
Let's go. I'll make you coffee.

01:02:42.842 --> 01:02:44.427
-Okay.
-All right.

01:02:46.972 --> 01:02:48.264
What happened?

01:02:49.099 --> 01:02:50.433
Did you get hurt?

01:02:50.517 --> 01:02:52.227
It's just a small scratch.

01:02:52.310 --> 01:02:53.436
[toy] Let's go on a walk.

01:02:53.520 --> 01:02:55.397
Let's go on a walk.

01:02:55.480 --> 01:02:58.274
[exclaims] We didn't get to go
on a walk today.

01:02:58.358 --> 01:03:00.485
You can go. I don't need coffee.

01:03:00.568 --> 01:03:02.404
I'll wait here for Mr. Seonu.

01:03:02.487 --> 01:03:03.530
Are you sure?

01:03:04.906 --> 01:03:06.408
Hey, Haran…

01:03:06.491 --> 01:03:08.952
About before…

01:03:09.995 --> 01:03:11.371
[hesitates] No, never mind.

01:03:11.955 --> 01:03:13.665
I'll be back soon.

01:03:13.748 --> 01:03:14.958
Wait a moment.

01:03:15.500 --> 01:03:18.795
cafe SHIM

01:03:19.379 --> 01:03:20.380
[sighs softly]

01:03:22.173 --> 01:03:23.508
Why isn't he coming?

01:03:28.638 --> 01:03:29.889
Oh?

01:03:29.973 --> 01:03:30.974
You're here.

01:03:34.978 --> 01:03:36.980
[♪ mellow music playing]

01:03:40.150 --> 01:03:42.110
[sighs] Where have you been this whole…

01:03:43.695 --> 01:03:46.072
Let's go inside. You look exhausted.

01:03:46.156 --> 01:03:47.490
[Chan] I'm sorry.

01:03:48.074 --> 01:03:49.617
For leaving like that

01:03:50.493 --> 01:03:52.328
and for hurting you.

01:03:53.913 --> 01:03:55.123
It's okay.

01:03:56.124 --> 01:03:57.709
I'm totally fine.

01:03:59.210 --> 01:04:00.420
It's all my fault.

01:04:00.962 --> 01:04:05.550
I was being selfish,
trying to stay by your side.

01:04:05.633 --> 01:04:06.718
What are you saying?

01:04:07.385 --> 01:04:09.763
Just make me some tea
instead of saying such nonsense.

01:04:15.185 --> 01:04:16.269
[sighs]

01:04:23.610 --> 01:04:24.611
[♪ music fades]

01:04:25.779 --> 01:04:27.781
I've been thinking…

01:04:28.823 --> 01:04:33.661
I don't think it's a good idea
for us to be this close, so--

01:04:33.745 --> 01:04:34.996
You saw this, right?

01:04:35.622 --> 01:04:38.041
Wow. I was so surprised when I saw it.

01:04:39.209 --> 01:04:42.712
These lines are where she mended
the broken pieces.

01:04:42.796 --> 01:04:45.131
Don't they make this look more beautiful?

01:04:45.882 --> 01:04:48.510
It seems admirable, too.

01:04:49.094 --> 01:04:50.970
-Ms. Song.
-To me…

01:04:53.932 --> 01:04:55.350
you're these lines.

01:04:56.226 --> 01:04:58.144
[♪ heartwarming music playing]

01:04:58.228 --> 01:04:59.521
[Chan] Ms. Song!

01:05:02.440 --> 01:05:03.817
[Haran] The first snow…

01:05:05.193 --> 01:05:06.277
Vapor trails…

01:05:06.361 --> 01:05:08.154
Wow, it's beautiful.

01:05:08.947 --> 01:05:10.448
Jamsugyo…

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:13.409
And a certain name…

01:05:14.327 --> 01:05:17.747
They were all sad memories,
so I thought I'd never get over them.

01:05:18.498 --> 01:05:21.417
But I found myself feeling okay,

01:05:22.418 --> 01:05:24.087
thanks to someone

01:05:25.088 --> 01:05:27.340
who covered them with good memories.

01:05:27.674 --> 01:05:28.758
[sighs]

01:05:28.842 --> 01:05:32.387
But you say something like that
over a tiny scratch?

01:05:32.512 --> 01:05:33.513
[scoffs]

01:05:34.264 --> 01:05:36.432
It's a relief I met you here.

01:05:38.184 --> 01:05:40.395
Thanks to you, I found a way,

01:05:40.979 --> 01:05:44.440
so this time, why don't you try it…

01:05:46.401 --> 01:05:47.443
with your father?

01:05:50.321 --> 01:05:51.739
That's impossible.

01:05:54.784 --> 01:05:56.578
You remember when we first met, right?

01:05:57.412 --> 01:06:00.248
I was cold and avoided you.

01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:03.585
I thought it was impossible too.

01:06:04.169 --> 01:06:08.339
But I guess there's no such thing
as never in a relationship.

01:06:09.090 --> 01:06:11.801
Aren't I a good example of that?

01:06:17.473 --> 01:06:19.434
I picked this up at the exhibit.

01:06:21.102 --> 01:06:23.021
He must wear this all the time.

01:06:23.104 --> 01:06:24.689
It's in the photo as well.

01:06:29.110 --> 01:06:30.236
I've never seen it before.

01:06:30.320 --> 01:06:31.529
Really?

01:06:32.405 --> 01:06:36.075
The drawing here looks similar
to the one I saw at your grandma's place.

01:06:41.372 --> 01:06:42.582
[sighs]

01:06:42.665 --> 01:06:46.502
[Haran] He must have kept wearing it
even when it was broken.

01:06:48.588 --> 01:06:50.423
I bought that for him a long time ago

01:06:51.549 --> 01:06:53.218
at a stationary store

01:06:54.427 --> 01:06:55.887
for Parents' Day.

01:06:56.846 --> 01:06:58.139
Maybe…

01:06:58.973 --> 01:07:01.142
he wanted to mend things.

01:07:01.726 --> 01:07:04.354
He's been wearing this broken watch
the whole time.

01:07:06.898 --> 01:07:07.899
[sighs]

01:07:08.566 --> 01:07:09.567
[♪ music fades]

01:07:14.948 --> 01:07:15.990
[sighs]

01:07:16.783 --> 01:07:18.743
[sighs] I should give you some time alone.

01:07:23.665 --> 01:07:24.832
Thank you.

01:07:29.796 --> 01:07:31.798
[♪ soft emotional music playing]

01:07:32.340 --> 01:07:33.549
[Haran sighs]

01:07:33.633 --> 01:07:38.429
I have a habit
of hugging people I want to comfort.

01:07:39.639 --> 01:07:41.224
That's my thing.

01:07:42.725 --> 01:07:44.060
Why do you keep copying me?

01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:50.233
I wish we'd met earlier.

01:07:51.109 --> 01:07:54.195
Then we could've gotten close faster,
and I would've been nicer first.

01:07:55.655 --> 01:07:58.157
I would have at least given you a hug

01:07:58.241 --> 01:08:01.119
when you were scared to open your eyes.

01:08:05.415 --> 01:08:06.874
[Chan sighs wearily]

01:08:06.958 --> 01:08:10.044
[laptop pinging]

01:08:10.628 --> 01:08:13.923
[Chan] You saved me as well.

01:08:14.007 --> 01:08:15.717
[rain pattering]

01:08:21.306 --> 01:08:24.642
You already did that for me.

01:08:31.024 --> 01:08:32.025
[sighs]

01:08:32.108 --> 01:08:33.109
[♪ music fades]

01:08:41.284 --> 01:08:46.873
[Chan] Genius, you know
that Haran should become happy, right?

01:08:47.665 --> 01:08:52.170
The fact that I lived
while he died from that accident…

01:08:52.253 --> 01:08:54.005
Her boyfriend died back then.

01:08:54.088 --> 01:08:56.591
He went to study in Boston,
but he suddenly died.

01:08:56.674 --> 01:08:58.676
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:09:01.929 --> 01:09:05.933
[in English] "Newbury Street, Boston?"

01:09:13.649 --> 01:09:14.650
[♪ music fades]

01:09:15.485 --> 01:09:17.362
[in Korean] I've only
received things from you.

01:09:21.366 --> 01:09:23.284
I should be really nice to you
from now on.

01:09:26.996 --> 01:09:28.039
Then…

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:32.710
I might end up liking you even more.

01:09:33.336 --> 01:09:34.879
It's okay…

01:09:36.214 --> 01:09:37.340
if you like me more.

01:09:39.509 --> 01:09:40.718
If I like you more…

01:09:44.597 --> 01:09:46.057
I might get more greedy.

01:09:49.560 --> 01:09:50.603
It's okay

01:09:51.854 --> 01:09:53.314
if you get more greedy.

01:10:01.322 --> 01:10:03.282
[♪ soft emotional song playing]

01:10:46.033 --> 01:10:47.952
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:10:48.035 --> 01:10:50.037
[♪ soft emotional song continuing]

01:11:12.059 --> 01:11:16.105
[Haran] Why do you keep saying
it's greedy to like me?

01:11:16.189 --> 01:11:18.566
-[Manjae] You mean it, right?
-[Chan] Yes.

01:11:18.649 --> 01:11:22.653
[Haran] How about letting time
with your dad start moving again?

01:11:22.737 --> 01:11:24.572
The past is the past,

01:11:24.655 --> 01:11:28.034
and what matters is the time you have now.

01:11:28.117 --> 01:11:30.578
[Hayeong]
There's nothing wrong with her, right?

01:11:30.661 --> 01:11:33.956
[Manjae]
What on earth is happening to you?

01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:36.918
[Chan] Seonu Chan found this pen for you.

01:11:37.001 --> 01:11:39.378
And this is a lucky charm.

01:11:39.462 --> 01:11:42.298
[Haran] No way. What is this?

01:11:46.302 --> 01:11:47.303
[♪ song fades]

01:11:48.387 --> 01:11:50.389
[♪ theme music playing]

01:11:56.270 --> 01:11:57.271
IN YOUR RADIANT SEASON

01:11:57.355 --> 01:11:58.356
Translated by Juyoung Park
